door areas are open daily from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.","source_url":"https://animalscience.uconn.edu/animal-barns/","source_title":"Visit the UConn Animal Barns | Department of Animal Science","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor areas of Livestock Unit I are open daily 10 a.m.–4 p.m.; buildings are not open to the public.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uconn-horsebarn-hill-trail-divide","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Horsebarn Hill Trail Divide","title":"Walk the Horsebarn Hill Trail Divide","subtitle":"Horsebarn Hill working-farm area, Storrs","notes":"Take a short walking loop, stay out of fields and pastures, pack out litter, and keep any dog leashed.","short_summary":"A named stop on UConn’s active farm landscape with field and wildlife context.","evidence_claim":"UConn’s Horsebarn Hill guidance invites visitors to enjoy the area and directs them to stay out of pastures, use established parking, and keep dogs leashed.","source_url":"https://hbh.uconn.edu/the-top/","source_title":"Top of Horsebarn Hill | Horsebarn Hill","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This is an active farm and wildlife habitat: obey posted signs, stay out of pastures, and use established parking areas.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uconn-uconn-forest-trailhead","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"UConn Forest Trailhead","title":"Take a UConn Forest walk","subtitle":"Trailhead at Horsebarn Hill","notes":"Download the forest map before leaving campus, choose a daylight route, and stick to passive recreation rather than entering managed work areas.","short_summary":"A trailhead into UConn-managed woodland used for teaching and local passive recreation.","evidence_claim":"UConn identi